Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:53:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Create the achievement toast only while it has something
 to show

The achievement notification dialog was created at startup and never
destroyed. While any ImGui dialog exists, the overlay requests a window
repaint every monitor refresh, so the window was presented at the monitor
rate (e.g. 144 Hz) instead of only when the guest presents a frame.

Now the dialog is created on the UI thread when an achievement event
arrives, and destroyed once its last toast has faded out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CGstJFihyJYNUGR3QC7gUu
